project/editor-floating-docks: spoint in-engine editor no longer obscures the game view. EditorShell.js shellView() main is a full-bleed .ds-ep-stage with .ep-viewport-pane (absolute inset:0, pointer-events:none) + a .ds-ep-dock-layer (pointer-events:none) holding two floating docks: .ds-ep-dock-left (Scene/hierarchy) and .ds-ep-dock-right (Inspector/tabs). The docks are the ONLY pointer-events:all elements, so the game canvas behind is visible AND click-through everywhere a dock isn't (witnessed: elementFromPoint at the exposed center returns CANVAS). Dock chrome (.ds-ep-dock/-head/-body/-title, .ds-ep-stage, collapsed state, mobile bottom-sheet @media max-width:760px) lives in anentrypoint-design editor-primitives.css: translucent background color-mix(in oklab,--panel-1 82%,transparent)+backdrop-filter:blur(10px). Collapse toggles via _leftCollapsed/_rightCollapsed -> header button shrinks dock to its head strip. Selecting an entity auto-expands the right dock. REPLACED the old viewport-squeezing C.SplitPanel(260px side|viewport|320px inspector) which used opaque var(--panel-1) panels. The old _ensureEditorResponsiveCSS mobile SplitPanel band rules (.ds-ep-split-pane:has(.ep-viewport-pane) order/40vh) were removed.